  "summary": {
    "intent": "Drive a set of stacked/parallel PRs (#519, #523, #526, #527, #497) through iterative review rounds using delegated subagents, resolving review findings so they can be merged in a sensible order.",
    "outcome": "#519 (lockfile fix) reached c4e0a44a with no open findings; #527 round 7 landed at 03589371 with all gates green, a code review returned nine items, and seven were sent to a new worker for round 8 while one was dismissed as a follow-up. Merge order is still pending.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "Root AGENTS.md rules: comments carry only the non-obvious why with no history (e.g. no 'On the base ...'), changeset bullets are one idea each and leave out internals.",
        "build.rs exports CALIPER_SEMANTIC_LOCKFILE from one lockfile() rule (workspace lock, else the crate's own); the pin test prints SKIPPED when no lockfile exists, so tests work from an unpacked `cargo package` crate.",
        "Gate suite for these PRs: just lint, doc-check, machete, typos, nextest, test-checker-lane, determinism, memory (~370 MiB), mantine/chakra diff vs main, and session_equals_cold.",
